<title>USA: GeoResources plans new well.</title>
<headline>GeoResources plans new well.</headline>
<dateline>WILLISTON, N.D. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>GeoResources Inc, which earlier Wednesday reported increased earnings for the first quarter, said it plans to start another horizontal well this month.</p>
<p>The company said the Ballantyne-State/Steinhaus H1 well is in North Dakota. GeoResources operates the well and owns a 100 percent working interest in its lease.</p>
<p>The well is planned for a horizontal lateral length of about 4,000 feet, GeoResources said.</p>
<p>Earlier the company said it earned $183,000, or $0.05 a share, compared to $114,000, or $0.03 a share, last year.</p>
